UPSTREAM — what this repository is derived from

Nothing third-party. This server is a client of a socket protocol, and the protocol belongs to
the workstation: the editor side is `IRSofkaStationCore`, the operator's own Unreal plugin,
installed at
  ~/Apps/LinuxUnrealEngine5.8.3/Engine/Plugins/Marketplace/IRSofkaStationCore/Source/

Every statement this file makes about the framing was READ from that source on 2026-10-15 and then
CONFIRMED by a live round trip against a running editor (roadmap item F11/STEP-0,
`tools/ue_bridge_probe.py`):

  IRSofkaDispatcher/Private/IRSofkaSocketServer.cpp
    - binds 127.0.0.1:9877
    - reads one request per connection, terminated by a newline
    - answers one JSON object with a newline appended
    - matches JsonObj->GetStringField("domain").ToLower() against registered handlers
    - runs handlers synchronously on the GameThread via FIRSofkaTaskRunner::ExecuteSync
  IRSofkaWorld/Private/IRSofkaWorldSubsystem.cpp
    - {"status":"SUCCESS"|"FAILED","error":...}
    - get_all_actors -> {status, count, actors:[{label,class,loc}]}
    - spawn -> {actor_label, class, location}; get_transform -> {location, rotation, scale}
    - set_transform -> {status} only

No code from the plugin, from any other MCP server, or from any engine SDK is in this tree: the
client here is stdlib Python that speaks the documented line protocol. A reading of a protocol to
interoperate with it is not a derivation of the implementation, and this file says so plainly so
nobody has to guess which side of that line the repository sits on.

Two defects found in the editor side by measurement are handled HERE rather than by editing the
plugin, because the plugin fix needs a module rebuild inside the operator's live session:
  1. a bare class name makes LoadClass return null and the handler silently fall back to AActor,
     which has no RootComponent, so transforms become no-ops while every call says SUCCESS;
     this server resolves short names to /Script/Engine.* and refuses to send what it cannot
     resolve.
  2. set_transform replies with a status and nothing else; this server reads the transform back
     and reports the landed values, `changed`, and `DEGRADED` when SUCCESS moved nothing.
Both are recorded upstream as roadmap item F11/STEP-0b (quest 301, status HUMAN, decision 55).

